# Fields, separated by one space: <name> <version> <sha256> <address>
# Vendor apt rows hash the signing key because upstream publishes no checksum for it; apt verifies package signatures.
# emcc hashes the downloaded archive because upstream publishes only crc32c.
# A two-field row pins a package of the base's Debian archive, whose signatures apt verifies.
# node: sha256 from https://nodejs.org/dist/v26.13.0/SHASUMS256.txt
node 26.13.0 5848553868b402d3fabb5b09270649977780a390f832155721025a08b5104455 https://nodejs.org/dist/v26.13.0/node-v26.13.0-linux-x64.tar.gz
# npm: sha256 of the registry tarball, which matches the sha512 integrity of https://registry.npmjs.org/npm/12.2.1
npm 12.2.1 228bd64aaef23270dbdbd2cf3d5ef5c467602ef38c4066246cef1984adab9a67 https://registry.npmjs.org/npm/-/npm-12.2.1.tgz
# pnpm: the standalone release file, not the npm tarball: the tarball fetches its native binary from the
# registry when it first runs, which a pod cannot do. sha256 is the digest GitHub states for the release asset (gh api repos/pnpm/pnpm/releases/tags/v12.16.1);
pnpm 12.16.1 565ff81174a14f6f7bd5d84c1b17e51031a80230d370a1fe24be5d16bd02a825 https://github.com/pnpm/pnpm/releases/download/v12.16.1/pnpm-linux-x64.tar.gz
# dart: sha256 from the .sha256sum beside the file in the dart-archive
dart 3.13.7 eb99aed266efbcb615c6ae21c12f52cfe935b9f208bccc5fea7f64c21e867229 https://storage.googleapis.com/dart-archive/channels/stable/release/3.13.7/sdk/dartsdk-linux-x64-release.zip
# go: sha256 of the linux-amd64 archive from https://go.dev/dl/?mode=json
go 1.27.3 65efbc80fdc1fa2cd2631cad5b481777a68e8725f34e89f50fc6ac714e379b40 https://go.dev/dl/go1.27.3.linux-amd64.tar.gz
# helm: sha256 from https://get.helm.sh/helm-v4.3.1-linux-amd64.tar.gz.sha256sum
helm v4.3.1 0403a88ae20913d11b10a2467b50087721fea7581736da6b9d3992f5357fe54b https://get.helm.sh/helm-v4.3.1-linux-amd64.tar.gz
# yq: sha256 is the SHA-256 column of the release file "checksums", ordered by its file "checksums_hashes_order"
yq v4.54.1 8e34fc298390875de416e6a4afcb8cabeceb25d9aa8506c1a2f9353cf702ea5f https://github.com/mikefarah/yq/releases/download/v4.54.1/yq_linux_amd64
# promtool must match the rendered Prometheus version; sha256 from the release file sha256sums.txt.
promtool 3.16.0 68727009472a2c02e1ff7f062fd5b3e637285bffc8fc2d340c76fb449d6e0f34 https://github.com/prometheus/prometheus/releases/download/v3.16.0/prometheus-3.16.0.linux-amd64.tar.gz
# gitleaks: sha256 from the release file gitleaks_8.30.1_checksums.txt
gitleaks v8.30.1 551f6fc83ea457d62a0d98237cbad105af8d557003051f41f3e7ca7b3f2470eb https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks/releases/download/v8.30.1/gitleaks_8.30.1_linux_x64.tar.gz
# powershell: sha256 from the release file hashes.sha256
powershell 7.6.9 1da6d6d6035d651f20e70ddee7c4c15ac6ab8b9fb40ee92240d91263f28a884b https://github.com/PowerShell/PowerShell/releases/download/v7.6.9/powershell-7.6.9-linux-x64.tar.gz
# kubectl must stay within one minor of its API server; sha256 from the .sha256 file beside the binary.
kubectl v1.35.10 c49a28f1f4efc4d475ed05f47f2ce8e563bf7bef69ed77fe1b924ea6d83b6327 https://dl.k8s.io/release/v1.35.10/bin/linux/amd64/kubectl
# kubeconform: sha256 from the release file CHECKSUMS
kubeconform v0.8.0 9bc2bffbf71f261128533edaf912153948b7ff238f9a531ae6d34466ec287883 https://github.com/yannh/kubeconform/releases/download/v0.8.0/kubeconform-linux-amd64.tar.gz
# rclone: sha256 from the release file SHA256SUMS; release key at https://rclone.org/KEYS.
rclone v1.75.2 349ac8fba6ff65d6247043f1750cdcb518ec5d500ef91463a10d37c0ccdf3702 https://github.com/rclone/rclone/releases/download/v1.75.2/rclone-v1.75.2-linux-amd64.zip
# emcc: the Emscripten release that emsdk installs, at the build hash that
# https://raw.githubusercontent.com/emscripten-core/emsdk/main/emscripten-releases-tags.json names for 6.0.13.
# Upstream publishes no sha256 for the file, only the crc32c 2944624a in the metadata of its storage object
# https://storage.googleapis.com/storage/v1/b/webassembly/o/emscripten-releases-builds%2Flinux%2Feb132757325583b787fe9414b09afea9442b72ad%2Fwasm-binaries.tar.xz
# so the sha256 is the one measured on that file.
emcc 6.0.13 cda6801012ff3319a539111826ed02a9abd7eff135c2ef261c8941caf5a3763e https://storage.googleapis.com/webassembly/emscripten-releases-builds/linux/eb132757325583b787fe9414b09afea9442b72ad/wasm-binaries.tar.xz
# skopeo uses Debian's signed package and runtime dependencies instead of an upstream release archive. Read at https://packages.debian.org/trixie/skopeo
# and in the trixie Packages index https://deb.debian.org/debian/dists/trixie/main/binary-amd64/Packages.xz. A newer build of the package replaces this
# one in the archive, so the build stops at this row until it is bumped
skopeo 1.18.0+ds1-1+b5
# These Debian packages preserve the system-Python ABI and the base's signed OpenSSH/runtime dependencies without a pip or source install.
# Sources: https://packages.debian.org/trixie/python3-bcrypt, https://packages.debian.org/trixie/openssh-server,
# https://packages.debian.org/trixie/bubblewrap and https://deb.debian.org/debian/dists/trixie/main/binary-amd64/Packages.xz.
python3-bcrypt 4.2.0-2.1+b1
openssh-server 1:10.0p1-7+deb13u4
bubblewrap 0.12.0-1~deb13u1
# The database clients come from the vendors' apt repositories on the base's Debian suite, because Debian's own archive carries one frozen
# series of each. The version of a row is the series of the database server the client dumps and restores, and the build installs a matching
# package of that series; test.sh holds the printed version to the series. Where the series says nothing about the client's own number, the row is
# the exact version. A server that leaves its series needs a new toolbox.
# mongodump (package mongodb-database-tools) and mongosh (package mongodb-mongosh): MongoDB's apt repository of the 8.0 series, named by the address of its
# signing key. The database tools (100.x) and mongosh (2.x)
# are numbered apart from the server, so the row is the exact version from the 8.0 repository for trixie
# (https://repo.mongodb.org/apt/debian/dists/trixie/mongodb-org/8.0/main/binary-amd64/Packages)
mongodump 100.20.1 8c467ea138207ee8d0cbbce3e005c82c73c81b3263e7909bdc36b9a1feff14f6 https://pgp.mongodb.com/server-8.0.asc
mongosh 2.14.1 8c467ea138207ee8d0cbbce3e005c82c73c81b3263e7909bdc36b9a1feff14f6 https://pgp.mongodb.com/server-8.0.asc
# mongod: package mongodb-org-server of MongoDB's apt repository of the 9.0 series for trixie
# (https://repo.mongodb.org/apt/debian/dists/trixie/mongodb-org/9.0/main/binary-amd64/Packages); the 8.0 repository for trixie carries no server package.
# The key is named by the major (server-9.asc), so the series of the repository is the major.minor of the version.
mongod 9.0.4 a8ec953b159e65ee2e327dde5506008d7693c3c6c3841beed421ec429bd10162 https://pgp.mongodb.com/server-9.asc
# pg_dumpall (with psql): package postgresql-client-18 of the PostgreSQL project's apt repository, https://apt.postgresql.org/pub/repos/apt trixie-pgdg
pg_dumpall 18 0144068502a1eddd2a0280ede10ef607d1ec592ce819940991203941564e8e76 https://www.postgresql.org/media/keys/ACCC4CF8.asc
# redis-cli (package redis-tools) and redis-server: Redis' apt repository, https://packages.redis.io/deb trixie, which carries every series. The version
# field of both rows is the marker REDIS_VERSION: the series is the ARG REDIS_VERSION of the Containerfile, which the consumer's version stamp writes
# and which the build pins both packages to. A restore starts a throwaway redis-server from the dump
redis-cli REDIS_VERSION 817b5a78358d00ed6b71884d70ad5d2eab9934badca1a34299fdc6a2e4a8ad20 https://packages.redis.io/gpg
redis-server REDIS_VERSION 817b5a78358d00ed6b71884d70ad5d2eab9934badca1a34299fdc6a2e4a8ad20 https://packages.redis.io/gpg
# mariadb (with mariadb-dump): package mariadb-client of MariaDB's apt repository of the 12.3 series,
# https://dlm.mariadb.com/repo/mariadb-server/12.3/repo/debian trixie
mariadb 12.3 403e0403df51273fbf5613e5644959d3f85923ef7d8f92e7d83eafe289093af4 https://supplychain.mariadb.com/mariadb-keyring-2025.gpg
